    "short_description": "Two brothers stuck in the world of computer games. They have to fix it to get out. An isometric homage to digital games culture and the art of playing together. Challenge your logic, cooperation and coordination.",
    "supported_languages": "English, Czech, Japanese",
    "reviews": "\u201cThe goal of the game isn\u2019t to connect with someone online and set off on a journey alone due to physical distance, but rather to meet up, sit in front of the same screen, and dive into the adventure together. More than once, I was reminded of the times spent with my own brother \u2014 the fratricidal battles in Bomberman or the extremely intense cooperation in Ugh! Pushmania brings back memories of what gaming used to be about, and what it still can be. Hats off.\u201d<br>4/5 \u2013 Level<br><br>\u201cBut that sweet feeling of satisfaction when you finally crack the code of a seemingly unsolvable map \u2014 after spending the last twenty minutes staring at the screen in frustration, trying every possible and impossible combination \u2014 that feeling is simply priceless. And that\u2019s exactly why we still play, hate, and love puzzle games like Pushmania.\u201d<br>8/10 \u2013 <br>",
